Attributions and provenance

Prayer times (src/Prayer/PrayerTimes.php)
  Written independently from standard astronomical equations: the low-precision
  solar position series of Jean Meeus, "Astronomical Algorithms" (as also used
  by the NOAA Solar Calculator), spherical-trigonometry hour angles, the
  standard -0.833 degree sunrise/sunset altitude, and the shadow-length
  definition of Asr. Per-method Fajr/Isha/Maghrib angles are published
  conventions (see resources/data/SOURCES.md). No third-party prayer-time source code
  was consulted or copied. Output was cross-checked against NOAA Solar
  Calculator sunrise/sunset values.

Reference data
  Bank BINs, Sheba bank codes, national-code prefixes, operator prefixes and
  the Umm al-Qura month table are factual data compiled from third-party
  public sources, listed in resources/data/SOURCES.md. The Umm al-Qura table was
  generated from ICU/CLDR calendar data (Unicode License,
  https://www.unicode.org/license.txt); no ICU source code is included.

Algorithms
  Luhn, ISO 7064 mod-97-10, the Iranian national-code checksum, the tabular
  Islamic calendar and Hebrew calendar arithmetic are public algorithms.

